60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have three options. A is per-room metering, B is a seasonal fixed rate, and C is a flat household share.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Option C is the simplest, but Option B might stop the monthly stress of fluctuating bills. Option A seems too expensive.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A sounds the most fair since I saw the monitor readings, but @May said it costs too much!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Exactly, Minato. Option A is out. Option C is easy, but the winter spikes are what I'm worried about.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Option A and B sound like they take a lot of time to manage. Option C is the fastest to calculate.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,Option B would allow us to stop doing arithmetic in our heads. We could just live and settle the difference once a year.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Daisuke, if we choose Option C, it's just a simple division. No one has to spend hours on a template.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"But if we do Option C, the people who use less power will still feel like they are carrying others!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, that's true, but Option B also has a year-end settlement. It just spreads the pain out.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I think Option C is the safest for the person doing the math. No templates, no meters, just one division.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,I value the peace of mind that comes with Option B. Not worrying about the heater in January is worth the year-end check.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,I want to avoid any system that leads to late payments or arguments. Option C is transparent and immediate.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I still think Option A is the fairest, but if we can't, maybe Option C is okay if we all agree?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,Option B is better for budgeting. I hate not knowing if my share will double in winter. I prefer the predictability.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm leaning towards C. It's the least amount of work for everyone involved.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,I will vote for Option B. Let us prioritize the feeling of the home over the precision of the yen.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I will vote for Option C. Simplicity is the best way to maintain our harmony and avoid conflict.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'll vote for Option C too. It's better than the current mess, and we can't afford the meters.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option B. I need to know what I'm paying each month without the winter shocks.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I vote for Option C. Please, let's just keep the paperwork as simple as possible.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
